Two articles I wrote with Amos are reproduced as appendixes to the book.
The first is the review of judgment under uncertainty that I described earlier.
The second, published in 1984, summarizes prospect theory as well as our studies of framing effects.
The articles present the contributions that were cited by the Nobel committee—and you may be surprised by how simple they are.
Reading them will give you a sense of how much we knew a long time ago, and also of how much we have learned in recent decades.
